@startuml trial-and-confirm
' The life of an image on the board: trial, confirmation, and the watchdog
' that reboots a board which stops making progress. Grounded in
' Src/watchdog.c, Src/confirm_record.c, Src/flash.c (flash_write_confirm_record),
' Src/ota_port.c and uart-flash-v1.md section 9, answers 4 and 5.

title An image on trial, and what makes it permanent

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Running

state Running {
  state "On trial" as Trial
  state "Confirmed" as Confirmed

  [*] --> Trial : no record in the last page\nof the running bank
  [*] --> Confirmed : the record is there\nAND names this version
  Trial --> Confirmed : CONFIRM\n/ write the record, ACK
  Confirmed --> Confirmed : CONFIRM again\n/ record already there, ACK
}

note right of Running
  The state is READ FROM FLASH on every INFO_REQ,
  never kept in RAM: a variable would say CONFIRMED
  again after each reset, which is the mistake the
  record exists to prevent. No record means
  unconfirmed (spec section 9, answer 4).
end note

note bottom of Trial
  **What erases a record**
  A mass erase of a bank takes that bank's record with it,
  which is right: the image it belonged to is being replaced.
  A power cut in the middle of the one double word leaves a
  half record, and a half record confirms nothing: the marker
  and the version are both checked.
end note

note top of Running
  **The watchdog runs in both states** (Bogdan, 2026-09-22).
  Started last at start-up and never stopped, fed every pass of
  the main loop, period about 32.8 s. It answers the failure the
  fault handler cannot: code that does not crash but stops making
  progress. A board stuck in the fault handler reboots after
  about 32 s instead of blinking forever.
  Rolling back to the other bank is the bank switch, piece 7.
end note

@enduml
